00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.410
So first, the M2 version,

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:55.470
the base M2 Mac mini is a game changer

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:56.880
because it's all the benefits

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.320
of the new Apple Silicon stuff,

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.600
the second-generation,
five-nanometer process,

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.160
the blazing fast shared memory,

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.440
all the optimizations that come with it,

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:08.940
for a starting price of $599, US.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.800
So I mean, it's a pretty simple computer,

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.820
not even a small tower,

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.070
just an absolutely tiny computer in there.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:15.540
It's basically the laptop,

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.730
but without the screen and the keyboard,

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:19.254
only one color, silver,

00:01:19.254 --> 00:01:21.600
and then a decent selection
of ports around the back,

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.540
along with a small exhaust
vent for active cooling,

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:25.770
and a headphone jack.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.000
And so this thing packs

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.090
a surprisingly enormous
power for its size.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.040
We've seen this Apple
Silicon transition play out

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.210
over the past two years.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:36.210
And when the Mac mini
moved to Apple Silicon

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:37.444
from the Intel chips,

00:01:37.444 --> 00:01:41.010
it took an absolutely hilarious
leap up in performance.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.440
Some of the numbers on
paper are just ridiculous.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.273
You have to forgive me

00:01:44.273 --> 00:01:46.740
for using Apple's stupid unlabeled charts,

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:48.930
but like, just to give you an idea,

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:51.270
this completely changed
the nature of the product.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.520
So this M1 Mac mini is
already dramatically better

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.650
than the Intel one for 99% of people.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:59.280
And now the M2 comes
along with more cores,

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:02.880
a more powerful CPU and
GPU, more max memory,

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.070
and a higher overall performance ceiling,

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:10.070
and the price goes down from $699 to $599.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:11.790
Apple almost never lowers the price

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:12.990
of the entry level of anything,

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.280
but that's exactly what's happened here.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.070
So we just got a computer
that's more powerful,

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:21.330
and more capable, and more
efficient for less money.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:23.783
And so then we also have
the M2 Pro Mac mini.

00:02:23.783 --> 00:02:26.070
This is the one that I've
been testing and using.

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:27.180
And so before, we just had

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:30.569
the base Apple Silicon M1
Mac mini, now that's the M2,

00:02:30.569 --> 00:02:32.820
but we've also now got this Pro chip,

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:36.780
which raises the ceiling
for Mac mini performance,

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:38.340
still on the same tiny body.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.500
Well, actually, I can't say
the exact same tiny body,

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.910
because the M2 Pro version

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:44.670
also does gain two more Thunderbolt ports.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.710
So now there's four Thunderbolt
four ports on the back

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:48.240
along with everything else still here.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:51.180
And that means you can now
do three external displays

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:52.380
instead of two,

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.720
and you can still option
up to 10 gigabit ethernet

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.120
if you're blessed with that
type of internet connection,

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.190
or if you're at an institution
that will take advantage

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.960
of the networking capability.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.240
And yes, that is HDMI 2.1.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.845
But the big deal here with
this new chip is the M2 Pro

00:03:05.845 --> 00:03:07.860
is so much more performant

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.440
thanks to the updated
architecture, and the extra cores,

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:14.310
that it's now benchmarking
actually over the M1 Pro

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:16.830
and the M1 Max in the CPU department

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:19.200
that was in the highest
end MacBook Pros before.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.790
I had to double take
when I first read that,

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:23.490
because M1 Max has been so incredible,

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:24.323
but yet here we are,

00:03:24.323 --> 00:03:26.970
even the incremental
improvements here are notable.

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:27.990
And on top of that,

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:30.240
the thermal advantage
potentially of a Mac mini

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:33.660
with active cooling in a taller
chassis over a MacBook Pro

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.460
can also mean in the long term, you know,

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:37.470
sustained CPU performance over time.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.240
You may see even better results there.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.210
So this thing's performance is rock-solid.

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:44.242
And then, of course, as you
move up in chips from base

00:03:44.242 --> 00:03:48.330
to Pro to Max, that's actually
mostly a GPU improvement.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.557
And so M2 Pro does great here, too,

00:03:50.557 --> 00:03:53.610
